----- a version that is not published [exit 4]
error[Z0710]: Zeff 0.9.5 is not published for linux-x86-64
  = help: published for it: 0.9.0, 0.9.1, 0.10.0-rc.1; a version before its release is installed only when it is named in full

----- a series with no release [exit 4]
error[Z0710]: no release of Zeff 0.10.x is published for linux-x86-64
  = help: published for it: 0.9.0, 0.9.1, 0.10.0-rc.1; a version before its release is installed only when it is named in full

----- a word that is no version [exit 1]
error: `zeff engine install` takes one version, as `zeff engine install 0.9.1`, a series, as `zeff engine install 0.9` for the newest 0.9.x, or nothing for the newest of all

run `zeff help` to see the commands

----- two versions [exit 1]
error: `zeff engine install` takes one version, as `zeff engine install 0.9.1`, a series, as `zeff engine install 0.9` for the newest 0.9.x, or nothing for the newest of all

run `zeff help` to see the commands

----- frozen [exit 4]
error[Z0710]: Zeff 0.9.1 is not installed, and nothing is fetched under `--frozen`
  = help: `zeff engine install --from <file>` installs an archive that is already on this machine

----- offline [exit 4]
error[Z0710]: an engine is asked for, and nothing is fetched under `--offline`
  = help: `zeff engine install --from <file>` installs an archive that is already on this machine

----- frozen by the environment [exit 4]
error[Z0710]: Zeff 0.9.1 is not installed, and nothing is fetched under `ZEFF_FROZEN`
  = help: `zeff engine install --from <file>` installs an archive that is already on this machine

----- no key built in [exit 1]
error[Z0711]: this launcher has no signing key built in, so it can prove no archive; nothing was unpacked
  = help: an official launcher carries the key its engines are signed with; this one was built from source before a key was published

----- a mirror that is not an address [exit 1]
error: the mirror is set to `mirror.univ.example`, which is not an address: it begins with `https://` or `http://`; it is set by `ZEFF_MIRROR` or by `[network] mirror` of `config.toml`

run `zeff help` to see the commands

----- the server fails [exit 1]
error[Z0708]: the engine index could not be fetched from `http://mirror/engines/index.toml`: the server answered 500
  = help: the launcher fetches from the mirror `http://mirror/`, set by `ZEFF_MIRROR` or by `[network] mirror` of `config.toml`; `zeff engine install --from <file>` installs an archive that is already on this machine

----- no index on the server [exit 1]
error[Z0708]: the engine index could not be fetched from `http://mirror/engines/index.toml`: the server has no such file
  = help: the launcher fetches from the mirror `http://mirror/`, set by `ZEFF_MIRROR` or by `[network] mirror` of `config.toml`; `zeff engine install --from <file>` installs an archive that is already on this machine

----- an index changed after it was signed [exit 1]
error[Z0711]: the signature of the engine index does not match it; nothing was unpacked
  = help: the file was changed after it was signed, or was cut short on the way; fetch it and its signature again

----- an index signed by another key [exit 1]
error[Z0711]: the engine index is signed with a key this launcher does not trust; nothing was unpacked
  = help: an engine is signed with the key built into the launcher or with a key on its signed key list; an archive from anyone else is refused, whatever it holds

----- an index of a later form [exit 1]
error[Z0717]: the engine index cannot be read: its `format` is not 1, the one this launcher reads; the store is as it was
  = help: the index is the publisher's and is faulty as published; `zeff report-bug` writes a report, and `zeff engine install --from <file>` installs an archive that is already on this machine

----- an index without its signature [exit 1]
error[Z0708]: the signature of the engine index could not be fetched from `http://mirror/engines/index.toml.minisig`: the server has no such file
  = help: the launcher fetches from the mirror `http://mirror/`, set by `ZEFF_MIRROR` or by `[network] mirror` of `config.toml`; `zeff engine install --from <file>` installs an archive that is already on this machine

----- an archive changed on the server [exit 1]
error[Z0711]: `zeff-0.9.1-linux-x86-64.tar.zst` is not the file that was published: its SHA-256 is d84303230589b47ddeebb874d3b973e2fdd4e7c3a1e621a9f07f8c7018169962 and the published one is 174a2ea1628e97d6f30c1a42c7cb6b39b5d7d7bc7ba407477c0825a29e15d318; nothing was unpacked
  = help: a download that stopped early gives this, and so does a file changed on the way; fetch the archive again

----- a release another key signed [exit 1]
error[Z0711]: `SHA256SUMS` is signed with a key this launcher does not trust; nothing was unpacked
  = help: an engine is signed with the key built into the launcher or with a key on its signed key list; an archive from anyone else is refused, whatever it holds

